# "This spell costs {X} less to cast, where X is the greatest mana value among Elementals you control": on turn 5 Bot1 controls Sandman (a Sand Elemental, mana value 3) and Bramble
# Familiar (an Elemental Raccoon, mana value 2): the greatest is 3, not their sum 5, so Sunderflock ({7}{U}{U}) costs {4}{U}{U} - six mana, and Bot1 has exactly six
# (three lands and three Moxen), leaving nothing in the pool. "When this creature enters, if you cast it, return all non-Elemental creatures to their owners' hands":
# Bot2's Guerrilla Gorilla (not an Elemental) goes back to Bot2's hand, while Bot2's own Bramble Familiar, Bot1's Sandman and Familiar, and Sunderflock itself (all Elementals)
# stay. Bot1's own Elementals are what make it cheap, so the ability never touches them.

